Do not beetmove stub installer in esr based releases r=jlund a=release DONTBUILD\n\nMozReview-Commit-ID: Cr10sPPv8Nd", "files": ["testing/mozharness/configs/beetmover/repacks.yml.tmpl"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "eac2f9584c149bcfd888746b4427790091e04002", "parents": ["324b9bea306f3802ac641c88446b4cfa51100579"], "tags": []}], "date": 1464907360, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "raliiev@mozilla.com"}, "159": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1272649 - Backport fix for erroneous 'flexible array member in union' to harfbuzz 1.1.0 on esr45 to avoid compilation failure with stricter compilers. r=jrmuizel, a=lizzard", "files": ["gfx/harfbuzz/src/hb-font-private.hh", "gfx/harfbuzz/src/hb-open-type-private.hh", "gfx/harfbuzz/src/hb-private.hh"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "a4acf1dd5b8f1270398bee4c53c707dc6399d67b", "parents": ["eac2f9584c149bcfd888746b4427790091e04002"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Terrence Cole \u003cterrence@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1007136 - Ensure malloc/free always match when using JSAutoByteString. r=bz, a=lizzard", "files": ["js/src/jsapi.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "5cb01593c52bf7062234305ef378fdd8d102731b", "parents": ["a4acf1dd5b8f1270398bee4c53c707dc6399d67b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jacek Caban \u003cjacek@codeweavers.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1263653 - Fixed TSFTextStore.h compilation with mingw. r=masayuki, a=lizzard", "files": ["widget/windows/TSFTextStore.cpp", "widget/windows/TSFTextStore.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "d27564cb37021d6988eb8e9592542afab89822a6", "parents": ["5cb01593c52bf7062234305ef378fdd8d102731b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jean-Yves Avenard \u003cjyavenard@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1267036 - Force recalculation of readyState when download is progressing. r=jwwang, a=lizzard\n\nUnder some circumstances, the MP3Demuxer is unable to calculate the buffered range which would prevent the readyState value to be recalculated. To get around this we force recalculation when the progress event is fired.\n\nMozReview-Commit-ID: DTaxJjOX4JU", "files": ["dom/html/HTMLMediaElement.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "1a1d754e809592aa50dea319d7e5b0dc7502b307", "parents": ["d27564cb37021d6988eb8e9592542afab89822a6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Patrick Brosset \u003cpbrosset@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1206345 - Force a state update in browser_animation_reconstructState.js. r=jdescottes, a=test-only\n\nThis test wasn't using refreshState, instead it used getCurrentState.\nWhat refreshState does on top of getCurrentState is it stores the new state\nlocally.\ngetCurrentState isn't meant to be called externally, it is only meant to be\nan actor method interceptor that reconstructs the missing state.\nSo the test should have used refreshState from the start.\n\nTurns out it worked in most cases because the animation did have a startTime\nwhen the test retrieved it, so it had a previousStartTime.\nBut, if for some reason, the animation has a startTime=null when the test\nstarts, then the value never gets to the front, and bad things happen.\n\nMozReview-Commit-ID: 2nEIKHMHsCS", "files": ["devtools/server/tests/browser/browser_animation_reconstructState.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "cc66722d5464b439b0220aad944dee435f35dfad", "parents": ["1a1d754e809592aa50dea319d7e5b0dc7502b307"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Matteo Ferretti \u003cmferretti@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1210208 - Intermittent browser_cmd_highlight_01.js | This test exceeded the timeout threshold. r=miker, a=test-only\n\nMozReview-Commit-ID: CIDclgvGylo", "files": ["devtools/client/commandline/test/browser.ini", "devtools/client/commandline/test/browser_cmd_highlight_01.js", "devtools/client/commandline/test/browser_cmd_highlight_03.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "dd1e614c5e71a6d7496740cfd73cb042e9c88924", "parents": ["cc66722d5464b439b0220aad944dee435f35dfad"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Neil Deakin \u003cneil@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 916004 - Set datasource after loading to see if intermittent orange of test_bug330010.xul goes away. a=test-only", "files": ["dom/xul/templates/tests/chrome/test_bug330010.xul"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "0a969f8e80a6d77fb00ecf7feec5053fe35aea5f", "parents": ["dd1e614c5e71a6d7496740cfd73cb042e9c88924"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Graham \u003cjames@hoppipolla.co.uk\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1215812 - Increase the internal timeout for a test that depends on a window opening. r=Ms2ger, a=test-only\n\nMozReview-Commit-ID: HzNYyHiehbU", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/browsers/windows/browsing-context-names/002.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/browsers/windows/browsing-context-names/002.html"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "7dea5981ba78ed39fc2e0f8a18d4b4b865077ef9", "parents": ["0a969f8e80a6d77fb00ecf7feec5053fe35aea5f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ben Kelly \u003cben@wanderview.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1228222 - Don't try to access ftp::/localhost to test \"unknown server\". r=asuth, a=test-only", "files": ["dom/tests/unit/test_Fetch.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "b5b01a6019d150258e443dfb95e70657140882e5", "parents": ["7dea5981ba78ed39fc2e0f8a18d4b4b865077ef9"], "tags": []}], "date": 1464986191, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "160": {"changesets": [{"author": "Robert Strong \u003crobert.bugzilla@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1271761 - app update patch for adding CPU features/detection to update URL. r=mhowell, a=sylvestre", "files": ["toolkit/modules/UpdateUtils.jsm", "toolki